     Vcron                                                            Vcron     NNAAMMEE           Vcron - Vcron - Daemon to execute scheduled commands      SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS           vcron     DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN           Vcron  should  be started from /h0/startup with an '&' to execute          it in the background.            Vcron  searches  for  a crontab-file for each member of the group          'Cron'  in  a  directory specified by the SysInfo-entry 'CRONDIR'          (or   if   you  have'nt  the  SysInfo  module  in  the  directory          /h0/SPOOL/VCRON  !).   The  group-file  should  be located in the          directory /h0/SYS, or /dd/SYS or /d0/SYS.            Those  crontab's  are  loaded  into  memory.  Vcron then wakes up          every  minute and checks whether one command should be run in the          current  minute.   If  the first character of your command-string          is  a  '-',  Vcron  mails  the  output  of  your  command to you.          Alternativly  you  can  specify in a variable MAILTO the receiver          of  the  mail;  this can be another user or an alias specifying a          complete  group  of users even on remote sites.  For that feature          Vcron  is  looking in the SysInfo-module for the entry 'mail'; if          the  entry  is  not  found  VCron forks /h0/ETC/CMDS/mail.  Vcron          starts  the mailer with following arguments: 'mail -s=VcronOutput          <destintation>'.            Before  starting  your  command  VCron  does  a  setuid() and and          change  the  current  directory to your -dir. Also Vcron sets the          following  enviroment variables : HOME, USER, SHELL. SHELL can be          overridden by specifying it in your crontab, HOME and USER not.       BBUUGGSS           Vcron  can't  mail  the  output  of  a  command,  if  you specify          IO-redirection in your crontab-entry.       FFIILLEESS           /h0/SYS/group, /dd/SYS/group, /d0/SYS/group     SSEEEE AALLSSOO           crontab     Page 1                                  Printed (00-xxx-1900 00:00:00)